Description: Replace every ErrorDialogHandler popup with a skin control
 ErrorDialogHandler is Mixxx's single shared route for "show the user an error"
 from any thread: the database, library import/export, broadcasting,
 recording, controller mapping script exceptions, and more all go through
 ErrorDialogHandler::errorDialog(), which built and exec()'d (for the common
 modal case) or show()'d (the rarer non-modal case, e.g. controller script
 errors) a real QMessageBox.
 .
 This kiosk build has no keyboard, mouse or touchscreen attached. A modal
 QMessageBox blocks the whole GUI thread - and every other error routed
 through this same handler - until it is clicked, which here never happens;
 a non-modal one just sits on screen, unclickable, for the rest of the
 session. Confirmed independently of load-failed-banner.patch, which only
 covers BaseTrackPlayer's own direct QMessageBox::warning() call - a
 separate code path that does not go through this handler at all.
 .
 errorDialog() now logs the message with qWarning() and raises
 [Library],app_error instead of building any dialog. The skin shows it as a
 banner; the controller's BACK button clears it with an ordinary
 ControlObject write, same mechanism as load_error. The per-key dedup list is
 cleared immediately (nothing keeps a banner "still showing" the way a real
 dialog would), so a recurrence of the same error is reported again rather
 than being silently swallowed for the rest of the session. stdButtonClicked
 is emitted synchronously with Close (never Ignore, which would silence the
 key for the session; never Retry, which would reload the controller
 mapping), so callers that wait for a click - only
 ControllerScriptEngineBase, which otherwise stays silenced on every further
 controller-script error once the first one shows - are released right away.
 A should-quit (critical/fatal) error still exits Mixxx, immediately rather
 than after a click that will never come, so the kiosk's restart loop
 (~/.xinitrc) brings it back up promptly instead of hanging indefinitely.
Author: GRV6 build (local)
Forwarded: no

